<h1>Example: The Living Standard</h1>

<h2 id=infrastructure>Infrastructure</h2>

<p>A <dfn data-x=concept-widget>widget</dfn> has a <dfn data-x=concept-widget-state>state</dfn>.</p>

<h3 id=widgets>Widgets</h3>

<p>To <dfn data-x=concept-widget-poke>poke</dfn> a <span data-x=concept-widget>widget</span>
<var>widget</var>:</p>

<ol>
 <li><p>Set <var>widget</var>'s <span data-x=concept-widget-state>state</span> to "poked".</p></li>
 <li><p>Return.</p></li>
</ol>

<div algorithm>
<p>To <dfn>unpoke</dfn> a widget <var>widget</var>, run these steps:</p>
<ol><li><p>Set <var>widget</var>'s state to "idle".</p></li></ol>
</div>

<h3 id=gadgets>Gadgets <code>&lt;gadget></code></h3>

<pre class=idl>[Exposed=Window]
interface Gadget {};</pre>

<p>A <dfn data-x=concept-gadget>gadget</dfn> is a <span data-x=concept-widget>widget</span> with a
<dfn data-x-href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node">node</dfn>, as in <ref>DOM</ref>.

<p>To <dfn>assemble</dfn> a <span data-x=concept-gadget>gadget</span>:</p>

<ol>
 <li><p>Let <var>node</var> be a new <span>node</span>.
 <li><p>For each <span data-x=concept-widget>widget</span> in it:
  <ol>
   <li><p><span data-x=concept-widget-poke>Poke</span> it.
   <li><p>See <a href="#widgets">widgets</a> and <a href="https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-tree">trees</a>.
  </ol>
</ol>

<p w-dev>A <dfn>developer note</dfn>, only in the developers' edition.

<h3 id=doohickeys>The <dfn id=doohickey>doohickey</dfn> section</h3>

<p>Each <span>doohickey</span> has a <code>gadget</code> (which isn't a cross-reference).
